  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Restoring and Managing Priority Habitats in Asuncin Bay</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Restore and manage 25 ha of priority habitats within Asuncin Bay, including the restoration of 8 ha of beach habitat, and the effective management of 17 ha of grassland habitat. Guyra Paraguay will hire and train two reserve guards to ensure effective protection and management of the area (522 ha), and will lead the update of the management plan. The project will also build on earlier NMBCA-support to raise awareness of the importance of the bay for migratory shorebirds.through developing and installing information panels at two visitor centers, and ongoing training of local conservation promoters, including as ecotourism guides and to work with local and national media</narrative>
  </description>
